Found in k242 (llm-advisor, 2026-09-25, docs only). Langertha::Engine::Replicate extends OpenAIBase with url https://api.replicate.com/v1, i.e. POSTs /v1/chat/completions. Replicate official OpenAPI (https://api.replicate.com/openapi.json, info.version 1.0.0-a1, fetched 2026-09-25) has NO chat/completions path: only /predictions, /models/{owner}/{name}/predictions, /deployments/.../predictions, /models, /collections, /files, /trainings, /hardware, /search, /account, /webhooks. replicate.com/docs/llms.txt has no OpenAI-compatibility page. Third-party 2026 comparisons state Replicate is not OpenAI-compatible. The OpenAI-compatible examples on replicate.com model pages (e.g. ibm-granite) are for running the Cog container locally, not the hosted API. Risk: engine may not work at all against the hosted API; POD claims "OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint". TODO: live-probe once a key is available (LANGERTHA_REPLICATE key empty until 2026-09-25 per memory), then either retarget to the predictions API (own format -> Engine::Remote) or document/deprecate. Not live-verified.

